  "title": "Repair the colonnade",
  "brief": "An old colonnade has lost some of its stones. A column stands on every fourth cell of the street, starting where you are, and each one rises to the stone beam above it. Fill every gap so each column is solid up to its beam, without stacking two stones in one cell, and finish at the east end facing east. Columns differ in height, and some are already whole.",
